for:**\\n- Violating principles you claim to defend (undermining your stated case)\\n- Tactics that predictably backfire (creating worse violence later)\\n- Shifting costs onto vulnerable populations who didn\\'t consent\\n- Avoiding accountability by claiming necessity\\n\\nThe honest tensions:\\n- Sometimes preventing *immediate* harm requires accepting *different* harms (genuine dilemma, not a free pass)\\n- \"Necessary to protect people\" is easy to assert, hard to verify beforehand\\n- Leaders have incentives to overstate necessity and understate costs\\n\\nWhat might actually matter more than \"unconventional vs. conventional\":\\n- Clear reasoning about *why* standard approaches fail *here*\\n- Honest accounting of tradeoffs, not hiding them\\n- Mechanisms to stop if assumptions were wrong\\n- Who bears the costs and whether they agreed\\n\\nWhat specific conflict context are you thinking about? The answer often depends heavily on details—what works (or fails) in diplomacy might be totally different from what works in immediate crisis management.', 'annotations': [], 'logprobs': []}], 'status': 'completed'}}, {'type': 'missing', 'loc': ('body', 'input', 'list[union[EasyInputMessageParam,Message,ResponseOutputMessageParam,ResponseFileSearchToolCallParam,ResponseComputerToolCallParam,ComputerCallOutput,ResponseFunctionWebSearchParam,ResponseFunctionToolCallParam,FunctionCallOutput,ToolSearchCall,ResponseToolSearchOutputItemParamParam,AdditionalTools,ResponseReasoningItemParam,ResponseCompactionItemParamParam,ImageGenerationCall,ResponseCodeInterpreterToolCallParam,LocalShellCall,LocalShellCallOutput,ShellCall,ShellCallOutput,ApplyPatchCall,ApplyPatchCallOutput,McpListTools,McpApprovalRequest,McpApprovalResponse,McpCall,ResponseCustomToolCallOutputParam,ResponseCustomToolCallParam,CompactionTrigger,ItemReference,union[ResponseOutputMessage,ResponseFileSearchToolCall,ResponseFunctionToolCall,ResponseFunctionToolCallOutputItem,ResponseFunctionWebSearch,ResponseCom